                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_579">Westminster, Middlesex.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Peter</orgName><p>Contains names of R. Teddington
                        and T. Gardener, monks of Westminster in s. xv. Marginal notes relating to
                        Westminster. <q>Liber ecclesie beati Petri Westmonasteriensi</q> or <q>Liber
                           Westmonasteriensi</q> is frequently written on the margins (RS ed. 1. xv)
                        at beginning and end and in the middle.</p><p>Compare the following footnote
                        in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), p. 167
                        n. 3: <q>Chetham 6712 belonged to Westminster abbey by s. xiii
                     ex.</q></p></provenance>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_474">St Albans, Hertfordshire,
                        Benedictine abbey of St Alban</orgName><p>This attribution was included in
                        the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), and there
                        were no relevant changes in the Supplement (1987). However, the attribution
                        appears to have been overlooked during MLGB3 (2010-2015). No corresponding
                        Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card was found during data
                        reconciliation work undertaken in 2026. There is a relevant footnote in the
                        second edition (1964), p. 167, n. 9:</p>
                     <p><q>These manuscripts contain writing in the hand of Matthew Paris: see R.
                           Vaughan, 'The Handwriting of Matthew Paris', <title>Trans. Cambr. Bibl.
                              Soc.</title>, i (1953), 390-92.</q></p></provenance>
               </history>
